# A single bare name is not an import — REFUSED

No `.expected`, so the front gate requires this to be refused.

`import credential` has no member to drop, so no module path can be derived from it. The refusal is
what keeps it from becoming an ordinary NAME: before the keyword was claimed, `import credential`
parsed as two statements and failed much later with `unknown name 'import'`, in a file and at a
line the reader did not write.

```scalascript
import credential

println("unreachable")
```
